---
description: Ban decorative em/en dashes and hyphen separators in user-facing UI copy
alwaysApply: true
---

# No hyphen / em-dash separators in UI

User-facing copy must **not** use decorative dashes as separators.

## Forbidden in UI strings (labels, headings, toasts, empty states, meta descriptions shown to users)

- Em dash: `—` (U+2014)
- En dash: `–` (U+2013)
- Spaced hyphen as a sentence break: ` - ` between clauses (e.g. `Cart empty - add books`)

## Allowed

- Hyphen **inside** compound words or codes: `look-inside`, `ISBN-13`, CSS `min-h-11`, `qty - 1` arithmetic
- Middot separators when needed: `·` (e.g. footer `Terms · শর্তাবলি`)
- Bangla danda / period: `।` or English `.` / `,` / `:`

## Prefer

```text
❌ বাংলাদেশের বইয়ের ঘর — পড়ুন
✅ বাংলাদেশের বইয়ের ঘর: পড়ুন

❌ BookVerse — Home
✅ BookVerse: Home

❌ Spoiler — tap to reveal
✅ Spoiler: tap to reveal
```

## Scope

Applies to `frontend/` Astro pages, React islands, UI components, and user-visible mock strings. Code comments may use plain ASCII `-` for lists; still avoid em/en dash in comments that mirror UI copy.
